  "notes": {
    "part:VR1": "Bass: clockwise boosts (to about +20 dB), anticlockwise cuts (about -20 dB), half-way is flat. C9 and C7 short the pot out at high frequencies, so it only acts on the bass.",
    "part:VR2": "Treble: clockwise boosts, anticlockwise cuts, half-way is flat. C12 and C11 pass only the treble to it.",
    "part:C1": "TI's input cap (C1, 2.2 µF, in front of its buffer: a 16 Hz corner there), moved to the network's input so the block takes a signal at any DC level.",
    "part:IC1": "The tone network sits in this op-amp's feedback, so cut and boost are symmetrical and the flat setting loses nothing. It inverts the signal."
  }
